<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="adenosine deoxyribonucleotides de novo biosynthesis I" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-7227" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Ubiquitous Plant Pathways (UPP) that was generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are thought to be present in all or most land plants. All UPP pathways are automatically imported into databases regardless of Pathologic predictions. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; Once |FRAME: ADP| is formed (see |FRAME: PWY-7219|) it can be converted to the deoxy form, |FRAME: DADP| (dADP), by the enzyme ribonucleoside diphosphate reductase. The enzyme can only accept ribonucleoside diphosphates, and is inacative with the mono- or triphosphate forms. dADP is phosphorylated to the DNA precursor |FRAME: DATP| (dATP) by the broad-substrate range |FRAME: NUCLEOSIDE-DIP-KIN-CPLX|.</Description>
